WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:08.430
Superman is indisputably the most powerful
superhero in the world. He's indestructible,

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:12.670
and wields the most comprehensive array of
superpowers imaginable, from super-hearing

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.320
all the way to super-ventriloquism. And he
does it all with a friendly smirk, just this

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.290
side of smug. But considering how tough Superman
is, there's still a surprisingly long list

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:27.700
of characters who have actually defeated him,
heroes and villains alike. How? Here's a look

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:32.719
at just a few of the characters who have knocked
the curl right off his forehead.

00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:34.250
Batman

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:40.410
On paper, Batman beating Superman seems impossible.
Unless that paper is between the covers of

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.830
a comic book. In that case, well, you can
pretty much write Superman's epitaph, because

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:50.760
Batman has time and again shown he has what
it takes to put Superman six feet under. Usually,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.960
of course, the World's Greatest Detective
wins thanks to the World's Greatest Cheat

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.360
Code, otherwise known as Kryptonite. Which,
ironically, Superman himself gave Batman as

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:06.329
a failsafe just in case Superman went rogue.
In The Dark Knight Returns comic book, Batman

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:11.110
also had a couple other tricks up his sleeve,
namely Green Arrow and a Soviet Union that

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:16.409
liked to drop nukes. That isn't really playing
fair, is it?

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.640
Doomsday

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.340
Spoiler alert, but in Batman v Superman, not
only does Batman beat Superman using Kryptonite,

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:28.030
Superman also gets killed by Doomsday—just
like what happens when the two fought in the

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:32.729
comics. Doomsday doesn't have any tricks or
anything. He's a one-note villain whose only

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:38.010
purpose in the comics is to kill Superman
using brute force. In the infamous Death of

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:43.619
Superman storyline, Doomsday did just that
as part of a spectacular double K.O. As villains

00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:47.909
go, Doomsday is pretty boring, but he got
the job done.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:49.140
The Avengers

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.229
Bet you weren't expecting to see the Avengers
on this list, with them being from a completely

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:57.400
different publisher and all. But Marvel's
mightiest heroes did indeed put the ultimate

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:04.189
smackdown on Superman in the pages of Avengers/JLA
#2. In this hotly contested inter-universe

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:10.060
crossover, Superman and Thor went toe-to-toe.
Superman barely beat Thor, but ended the fight

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:15.019
dazed and severely weakened. That was more
than enough of an opening for Thor's Avenger

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:20.669
buddies to do what they do best: Avenge him.
The team's heaviest hitters, Iron Man, Hercules,

00:02:20.669 --> 00:02:27.150
Wonder Man, The Vision, and She-Hulk, dogpiled
on Superman and pummeled him unconscious.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:27.730
Lex Luthor

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:33.519
Superman's archenemy Lex Luthor has defeated
Superman so many times it's kind of hard to

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:38.349
just pick one example. Our favorite instance
of Lex dropping the hammer on Superman comes

00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:44.779
from the classic Superman #149, where Lex
wins Superman's trust… by curing cancer.

00:02:44.779 --> 00:02:49.299
With Superman convinced that Lex has reformed,
it’s easy for Luthor to trick Superman into

00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:55.069
a fatal Kryptonite trap. Supergirl later brought
Lex to justice for Superman's murder. It's

00:02:55.069 --> 00:03:00.669
a sad story, but on the other hand, Lex cured
cancer. Sorry, Supes, but that's not really

00:03:00.669 --> 00:03:03.049
a bad tradeoff in our book.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:03.379
Mongul

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:08.980
Superman's most dangerous foe may be Mongul,
who’s basically what you would get if you

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:14.069
combined Doomsday's incredible strength with
Lex Luthor's genius. Mongul has repeatedly

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:18.879
gotten the better of Superman, beating him
both physically and psychologically. Case

00:03:18.879 --> 00:03:24.999
in point: the classic Superman Annual #11
by Watchmen writer Alan Moore, in which Mongul

00:03:24.999 --> 00:03:31.370
traps Superman inside his own dreams. Luckily
for Superman and Earth at large, Robin defeats

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:37.529
Mongul. Yes, Robin. We're not sure who should
be more embarrassed, Superman or Mongul.

00:03:37.529 --> 00:03:39.870
Captain Marvel

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:46.079
Superman pretty much has only two major weaknesses:
Kryptonite and magic. Unfortunately for him,

00:03:46.079 --> 00:03:50.949
there’s Captain Marvel, who's alternately
known as Shazam...depending on whether DC

00:03:50.949 --> 00:03:54.859
Comics wants to publish stories about a dude
with the word "Marvel" in his name that day.

00:03:54.859 --> 00:04:00.269
He’s not only just as powerful as Superman,
but he got those powers from a super wizard—meaning

00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:05.629
he's powered by magic. That gives Captain
Marvel a pretty significant leg up on Superman.

00:04:05.629 --> 00:04:11.199
The two have fought numerous times. Usually,
Superman often wins in the end...because Captain

00:04:11.199 --> 00:04:13.719
Marvel is actually a little kid in an adult
body.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.100
"Shazam!"

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.660
But, the Big Red Cheese has knocked Supes
out more than once, and has even taken Superman

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.500
out with some well-timed bolts of magic lightning.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:28.900
"Shazam."

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.200
Atlas

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:37.190
Speaking of people with magic on their side,
there's Atlas. That's right, this dumb-looking

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:41.690
dork is actually the same guy who carried
the world on his shoulders in Greek mythology.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:46.940
Well, in the comics, he's… well, there's
no way to explain it that makes any sense,

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:54.450
so just trust us when we say that he's a really
strong dude. And in Superman #677 to #680,

00:04:54.450 --> 00:05:00.100
Atlas absolutely pounded the tar out of Superman.
And he did the same to everyone who tried

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:04.940
to stop him. Luckily for Superman, he had
an ally much, much tougher than even the Man

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:10.570
of Steel: Krypto the Superdog. Where Superman
failed miserably, Krypto succeeded, taking

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:15.840
Atlas down and saving Metropolis and the world.
Good doggie!

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.280
Green Lantern

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:23.940
Remember how Superman is vulnerable to Kryptonite?
Well, usually that's not such a big deal thanks

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:28.580
to the fact that there's not all that much
of it around. However, way back in DC Comics

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:35.120
Presents #26, a villain posing as Hal Jordan,
the Green Lantern of Earth, discovered a loophole.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.910
The Green Lantern ring can actually create
a form of synthetic Kryptonite. Once the real

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:44.740
Green Lantern knocked the bad guy out, the
fake Kryptonite disappeared. And eventually,

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:49.360
the power of Kryptonite-creation was removed
by comic book writers on account of it being,

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:54.920
well, ridiculous. But Green Lantern eventually
found another way to take Superman out. He

00:05:54.920 --> 00:06:00.310
bonded with the alien entity named Parallax
and became an omnipotent evil god. Hey, if

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:02.860
you can't beat 'em, join 'em.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:04.360
The Joker

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:09.150
Even though the Joker has yet to figure out
a way to defeat a rich playboy in a bat mask,

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:14.080
he's somehow defeated Superman multiple times.
For instance, in Emperor Joker, the Joker

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.620
stole the powers of Mr. Mix…

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.640
Uh...Mr. Mix-el-plick...

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.650
Um.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.670
"Mr. Mixel...plick?"

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:33.080
"No! Repeat after me, bright boy. It's Mxyzptlk."

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:42.140
Yeah, that guy. The Joker stole his powers
and reshaped reality. That included sealing

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:48.170
Superman away in Arkham Asylum. Shoe's on
the other foot now! Meanwhile, in the Injustice:

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:52.430
Gods Among Us video game, the Joker tricks
Superman into murdering Lois Lane.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:07:00.600
"I know it's soon... But think you'll ever
love again? Maybe you won't kill your next

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.700
family."

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:07.200
Then... the Joker nukes Metropolis. You know
what? That's not actually funny. Effective,

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.740
but not funny. Yuck.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:10.430
Muhammad Ali

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:16.360
Finally, we come to the greatest. For many
people, Muhammad Ali was as close to a real-life

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:20.710
superhero as we'll ever get, so it doesn't
come as a huge surprise to learn that he once

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:26.440
laid out Superman. The fight took place in
the aptly titled Superman vs. Muhammad Ali.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:31.480
An alien army attacks Earth and proposes a
simple contest of champions to determine the

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:35.880
fate of the world. To decide who should be
Earth's representative, Ali and Superman have

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:41.370
a boxing match, with Superman fighting without
his superpowers. So, it was essentially Ali

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:48.310
versus nerdy weakling Clark Kent. So what
happened? Ali knocked Superman senseless.

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:53.370
In the end, Ali also defeated the alien champion
in single combat, saving the planet.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:58.060
And all this fresh off his battle against
Mr. Tooth Decay.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:01.800
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:06.580
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know how you would kick Superman’s butt...

